# The app's name: the browser tab, and the home screen on iPhone (the manifest has its own copy).
VITE_APP_TITLE=かみわたし

# Settings of your own environment go in `.env.local` next to this file (gitignored), never here:
# this file is public.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL: the API's URL (default `/api`, on the web app's own origin: deployed, one
# Worker serves both; the Vite dev server proxies it to `wrangler dev`). Leave it unset unless the
# API is elsewhere on the same site: the browser only sends the sign-in cookie within the site.
#
# VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID: your Google sign-in web OAuth client id, with the web app's origin
# among its authorized JavaScript origins. Not secret (it ships in the app). The API accepts it as
# the ID token's `aud` (`GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS` in apps/backend-worker/.dev.vars, or `wrangler secret
# put` when deployed). Unset = the Google button stays disabled.
#
# VITE_OPERATOR_NAME / VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL: the operator's name and the contact address shown in the
# terms of use and privacy policy (`src/legal/documents.ts`). Set them before deploying; unset, the
# documents show placeholders.
